      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4191_Start3" name="BCP cycle (VS-26); disaster (VS-69); critical-system failure">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4191_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4191_Task4" name="Facilities/BCP identify critical building systems per site (power/generator…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Facilities/BCP identify critical building systems per site (power/generator, fire/life-safety, security, key HVAC, water) and their failure impact, aligned to BCP (VS-26.1)
Responsible (R): Facilities Maintenance Lead / BCP
Accountable (A): Head of Facilities
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4191_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4191_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4191_Task5" name="Facilities ensure resilience (generator backup, fire-system redundancy, BMS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Facilities ensure resilience (generator backup, fire-system redundancy, BMS fail-safe, spare-parts stock, provider SLA) and test failover periodically (links to VS-26.1 BCP testing)
Responsible (R): Facilities Maintenance Lead / Providers
Accountable (A): Head of Facilities
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4191_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4191_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4191_Task6" name="Facilities respond to critical-system failure/disaster (typhoon VS-69, fire…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Facilities respond to critical-system failure/disaster (typhoon VS-69, fire, flood, outage) per emergency procedures (VS-24.2/VS-26.2), recover, and capture lessons
Responsible (R): Facilities Maintenance Lead / BCP / HSE
Accountable (A): Head of Facilities
Duration: Reactive</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4191_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4191_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4191_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
